  'tutorial.chapter.start': "Start", 'tutorial.chapter.build': "Building a model", 'tutorial.chapter.run': "Running and animation", 'tutorial.chapter.analyse': "Analysis and experiments", 'tutorial.chapter.paradigms': "SD, agents, traffic", 'tutorial.chapter.help': "Files and settings",
  'tutorial.welcome.title': "Welcome to MyProductionFlow", 'tutorial.welcome.text': "Draw the flow of a factory, warehouse or road network with blocks and simulate it. Press Next to see every feature in turn.",
  'tutorial.templates.title': "Templates", 'tutorial.templates.text': "Start straight away from a basic process, conveyor, warehouse, traffic, system dynamics or agent template.",
  'tutorial.samples.title': "Sample models", 'tutorial.samples.text': "60 samples (10 per group): manufacturing, logistics, services, traffic, rail, pedestrians, SD, fluids and agents. Click one to open it; F5 runs it.",
  'tutorial.workspace.title': "The workspace", 'tutorial.workspace.text': "Left: the block library. Centre: the 2D editor and the 3D view. Right: the model list and properties. Bottom: statistics, charts, problems and experiments.",
  'tutorial.library.title': "Library", 'tutorial.library.text': "137 blocks in 12 categories: process, machines, handling, warehouse, traffic, rail, pedestrians, fluids, SD, agents, analysis, layout. Drag one onto the canvas, or click it and then click where it goes.",
  'tutorial.place.title': "Placing blocks", 'tutorial.place.text': "Click where the block goes. With one block selected, the new one is connected to it automatically. Conveyors, roads and walls take one click per point.",
  'tutorial.connect.title': "Connecting", 'tutorial.connect.text': "Drag a block's green dot (output) onto the next block to connect them. With the connect tool (C), drag from block to block.",
  'tutorial.properties.title': "Properties", 'tutorial.properties.text': "Edit the process time distribution (with a histogram preview), capacity, workers, reject rate and breakdowns (MTBF, MTTR) right here.",
  'tutorial.explorer.title': "Model list", 'tutorial.explorer.text': "Every block by category. Click to select, double-click to go to it.",
  'tutorial.problems.title': "Model check", 'tutorial.problems.text': "Unconnected outputs, wrong expressions, missing pools and more are found while you edit. Click one to go to the block.",
  'tutorial.runbar.title': "Run bar", 'tutorial.runbar.text': "Run (F5), step one event (F6), stop, run to the end (F7). It shows model time, progress, events and speed.",
  'tutorial.view2d.title': "2D animation", 'tutorial.view2d.text': "Entities move, and blocks show their state colour (busy green, idle yellow, blocked orange, failed red) and a utilization bar. The red lines on the top and left rulers mark the mouse; the 5 × 5 grid keeps its size while you zoom. The red circle in the run bar records the animation as a video.",
  'tutorial.view3d.title': "3D animation", 'tutorial.view3d.text': "The same model in 3D. Drag to orbit, right-drag to pan, wheel to zoom. Blocks can be picked and moved in 3D too. The eye button in the run bar makes the camera follow an entity.",
  'tutorial.speed.title': "Speed", 'tutorial.speed.text': "How much model time passes per second. The [ and ] keys change it too.",
  'tutorial.live.title': "Live statistics", 'tutorial.live.text': "Select a block while running to see its utilization, waiting and throughput live.",
  'tutorial.stats.title': "Statistics", 'tutorial.stats.text': "Throughput, cycle time, WIP and bottleneck cards, advice, and tables for stations, queues and handling.",
  'tutorial.charts.title': "Charts", 'tutorial.charts.text': "The model's charts, WIP and output, a station state timeline and the cycle time distribution. Add chart plots any value.",
  'tutorial.experiment.title': "Experiments", 'tutorial.experiment.text': "Parameter variation, Monte Carlo replications, optimization, sensitivity analysis (tornado) and multi-parameter optimization run the model many times to find the best value. Save runs as scenarios to compare them side by side.",
  'tutorial.report.title': "Report", 'tutorial.report.text': "A report with settings, results, advice and charts to print or save as HTML or CSV.",
  'tutorial.sd.title': "System dynamics", 'tutorial.sd.text': "Stocks, flows and parameters make continuous models (Bass diffusion). Equations use the names; parameters change with sliders while running.",
